#: ../../../docs/architecture.md:2
msgid "Architecture"
msgstr "Architecture"

#: ../../../docs/architecture.md:4
msgid "Boundary"
msgstr "Boundary"

#: ../../../docs/architecture.md:6
msgid "`magshield-env` converts explicit physical inputs into a validated, self-contained Gymnasium environment package. It does not design coils, invoke finite-element software, train policies, or know any experiment-specific directory layout."
msgstr "`magshield-env` converts explicit physical inputs into a validated, self-contained Gymnasium environment package. It does not design coils, invoke finite-element software, train policies, or know any experiment-specific directory layout."

#: ../../../docs/architecture.md:11
msgid "Components and dependency direction"
msgstr "Components and dependency direction"

#: ../../../docs/architecture.md:19
msgid "The domain layer has no dependency on terminal or Gymnasium code. Physics code accepts SI arrays and returns SI arrays. The Gymnasium layer consumes a plant interface and never reads source export formats. The TUI only gathers values and calls the builder API."
msgstr "The domain layer has no dependency on terminal or Gymnasium code. Physics code accepts SI arrays and returns SI arrays. The Gymnasium layer consumes a plant interface and never reads source export formats. The TUI only gathers values and calls the builder API."

#: ../../../docs/architecture.md:24
msgid "Core invariants"
msgstr "Core invariants"

#: ../../../docs/architecture.md:26
msgid "Points are shaped `[N, 3]` and response matrices `[N, 3, M]` in `float64`."
msgstr "Points are shaped `[N, 3]` and response matrices `[N, 3, M]` in `float64`."

#: ../../../docs/architecture.md:27
msgid "Coordinates are metres, field is tesla, current is ampere, time is seconds, resistance is ohm, and voltage is volt unless an importer declares and records an explicit conversion."
msgstr "Coordinates are metres, field is tesla, current is ampere, time is seconds, resistance is ohm, and voltage is volt unless an importer declares and records an explicit conversion."

#: ../../../docs/architecture.md:30
msgid "Point order, channel order, coordinate frame, array shape, and content hashes are bound in `manifest.json`."
msgstr "Point order, channel order, coordinate frame, array shape, and content hashes are bound in `manifest.json`."

#: ../../../docs/architecture.md:32
msgid "Finite-element channel files must describe the same points. Reordering is only allowed through an explicit, unique point identity or an explicit coordinate tolerance recorded in the build configuration."
msgstr "Finite-element channel files must describe the same points. Reordering is only allowed through an explicit, unique point identity or an explicit coordinate tolerance recorded in the build configuration."

#: ../../../docs/architecture.md:35
msgid "Dynamic geometry keeps conductors fixed in their declared frame, transforms body-frame points with the declared pose, and recomputes the analytic segment field. It never substitutes a fixed matrix."
msgstr "Dynamic geometry keeps conductors fixed in their declared frame, transforms body-frame points with the declared pose, and recomputes the analytic segment field. It never substitutes a fixed matrix."

#: ../../../docs/architecture.md:38
msgid "Hardware projection is observable through `info`; no illegal action is silently clipped."
msgstr "Hardware projection is observable through `info`; no illegal action is silently clipped."

#: ../../../docs/architecture.md:40
msgid "Export succeeds atomically only after every contract has passed."
msgstr "Export succeeds atomically only after every contract has passed."

#: ../../../docs/architecture.md:42
msgid "Data flow"
msgstr "Data flow"

#: ../../../docs/architecture.md:44
msgid "The builder resolves YAML input, creates or imports points, constructs either a fixed response or conductor geometry, validates hardware and scenario data, and writes canonical HDF5/YAML files plus their manifest. `make_env` reads only this package. At each `step`, the plant returns a response matrix for the active pose, the hardware model maps normalized current deltas into the legal interval, and the environment returns residual field, reward, termination state, and explicit constraint evidence."
msgstr "The builder resolves YAML input, creates or imports points, constructs either a fixed response or conductor geometry, validates hardware and scenario data, and writes canonical HDF5/YAML files plus their manifest. `make_env` reads only this package. At each `step`, the plant returns a response matrix for the active pose, the hardware model maps normalized current deltas into the legal interval, and the environment returns residual field, reward, termination state, and explicit constraint evidence."

