#: ../../../docs/decisions/0001-canonical-formats.md:2
msgid "0001: Canonical scientific exchange formats"
msgstr "0001: Canonical scientific exchange formats"

#: ../../../docs/decisions/0001-canonical-formats.md:4 ../../../docs/decisions/0002-gymnasium-contract.md:4 ../../../docs/decisions/0003-runtime-geometry.md:4 ../../../docs/decisions/0004-textual-tui.md:4
msgid "**Status**: accepted"
msgstr "**Status**: accepted"

#: ../../../docs/decisions/0001-canonical-formats.md:5 ../../../docs/decisions/0002-gymnasium-contract.md:5 ../../../docs/decisions/0003-runtime-geometry.md:5 ../../../docs/decisions/0004-textual-tui.md:5
msgid "**Date**: 2026-08-01"
msgstr "**Date**: 2026-08-01"

#: ../../../docs/decisions/0001-canonical-formats.md:6
msgid "**Context**: Users need files readable from Python, MATLAB, finite-element exports, and common visualization tools without binding the environment to one solver."
msgstr "**Context**: Users need files readable from Python, MATLAB, finite-element exports, and common visualization tools without binding the environment to one solver."

#: ../../../docs/decisions/0001-canonical-formats.md:9
msgid "**Decision**: In the need for cross-language scientific exchange, facing large dense arrays and geometric paths, we choose YAML/JSON Schema, HDF5, CSV, and VTK/VTP instead of project-private NumPy files, gaining explicit metadata and interoperability while accepting additional import dependencies."
msgstr "**Decision**: In the need for cross-language scientific exchange, facing large dense arrays and geometric paths, we choose YAML/JSON Schema, HDF5, CSV, and VTK/VTP instead of project-private NumPy files, gaining explicit metadata and interoperability while accepting additional import dependencies."

#: ../../../docs/decisions/0001-canonical-formats.md:13
msgid "**Consequences**: Canonical bundles remain portable; importers must perform strict shape, unit, and identity validation."
msgstr "**Consequences**: Canonical bundles remain portable; importers must perform strict shape, unit, and identity validation."

#: ../../../docs/decisions/0001-canonical-formats.md:15
msgid "**Alternatives Considered**: NumPy-only artifacts were rejected because they do not provide a sufficient cross-language metadata contract. Parquet was deferred because it does not improve the v1 scientific array boundary."
msgstr "**Alternatives Considered**: NumPy-only artifacts were rejected because they do not provide a sufficient cross-language metadata contract. Parquet was deferred because it does not improve the v1 scientific array boundary."

#: ../../../docs/decisions/0002-gymnasium-contract.md:2
msgid "0002: Gymnasium public environment contract"
msgstr "0002: Gymnasium public environment contract"

#: ../../../docs/decisions/0002-gymnasium-contract.md:6
msgid "**Context**: The exported result must be consumable by mainstream reinforcement-learning libraries without embedding training code."
msgstr "**Context**: The exported result must be consumable by mainstream reinforcement-learning libraries without embedding training code."

#: ../../../docs/decisions/0002-gymnasium-contract.md:8
msgid "**Decision**: In the need for a standard single-agent interface, facing the cost of maintaining a private protocol, we choose Gymnasium `reset/step` over a custom environment API, gaining ecosystem compatibility while accepting Gymnasium as a runtime dependency."
msgstr "**Decision**: In the need for a standard single-agent interface, facing the cost of maintaining a private protocol, we choose Gymnasium `reset/step` over a custom environment API, gaining ecosystem compatibility while accepting Gymnasium as a runtime dependency."

#: ../../../docs/decisions/0002-gymnasium-contract.md:12
msgid "**Consequences**: Observation and action spaces are explicit and tested; the package still contains no trainer or algorithm integration."
msgstr "**Consequences**: Observation and action spaces are explicit and tested; the package still contains no trainer or algorithm integration."

#: ../../../docs/decisions/0002-gymnasium-contract.md:14
msgid "**Alternatives Considered**: A private reset/step protocol was rejected because every downstream user would need an adapter."
msgstr "**Alternatives Considered**: A private reset/step protocol was rejected because every downstream user would need an adapter."

#: ../../../docs/decisions/0003-runtime-geometry.md:2
msgid "0003: Runtime geometry response"
msgstr "0003: Runtime geometry response"

#: ../../../docs/decisions/0003-runtime-geometry.md:6
msgid "**Context**: Head or sensor motion changes where a fixed winding is evaluated, so a fixed response matrix cannot faithfully describe every pose."
msgstr "**Context**: Head or sensor motion changes where a fixed winding is evaluated, so a fixed response matrix cannot faithfully describe every pose."

#: ../../../docs/decisions/0003-runtime-geometry.md:8
msgid "**Decision**: In the need for moving-grid environments, facing high repeated field-computation cost, we choose analytic finite-segment Biot-Savart with an identity-bound pose cache instead of fixed-matrix fallback or interpolation, gaining physical fidelity while accepting greater per-step cost."
msgstr "**Decision**: In the need for moving-grid environments, facing high repeated field-computation cost, we choose analytic finite-segment Biot-Savart with an identity-bound pose cache instead of fixed-matrix fallback or interpolation, gaining physical fidelity while accepting greater per-step cost."

#: ../../../docs/decisions/0003-runtime-geometry.md:12
msgid "**Consequences**: Dynamic packages must include conductor geometry; repeated exact poses can reuse computed responses, but unseen poses are recomputed."
msgstr "**Consequences**: Dynamic packages must include conductor geometry; repeated exact poses can reuse computed responses, but unseen poses are recomputed."

#: ../../../docs/decisions/0003-runtime-geometry.md:14
msgid "**Alternatives Considered**: Silent fixed-matrix fallback and nearest-pose interpolation were rejected because they change the declared physical model."
msgstr "**Alternatives Considered**: Silent fixed-matrix fallback and nearest-pose interpolation were rejected because they change the declared physical model."

#: ../../../docs/decisions/0004-textual-tui.md:2
msgid "0004: Textual as the interactive front end"
msgstr "0004: Textual as the interactive front end"

#: ../../../docs/decisions/0004-textual-tui.md:6
msgid "**Context**: Environment construction requires revisiting several related sections and reviewing errors before export."
msgstr "**Context**: Environment construction requires revisiting several related sections and reviewing errors before export."

#: ../../../docs/decisions/0004-textual-tui.md:8
msgid "**Decision**: In the need for a navigable terminal workflow, facing the limits of a one-way prompt sequence, we choose Textual over raw `input()` prompts, gaining editable screens and testable UI state while accepting one UI dependency."
msgstr "**Decision**: In the need for a navigable terminal workflow, facing the limits of a one-way prompt sequence, we choose Textual over raw `input()` prompts, gaining editable screens and testable UI state while accepting one UI dependency."

#: ../../../docs/decisions/0004-textual-tui.md:12
msgid "**Consequences**: TUI logic remains a thin client of the same builder API used by automation."
msgstr "**Consequences**: TUI logic remains a thin client of the same builder API used by automation."

#: ../../../docs/decisions/0004-textual-tui.md:14
msgid "**Alternatives Considered**: A sequential prompt wizard was rejected because users cannot efficiently review and revise a complete physical definition."
msgstr "**Alternatives Considered**: A sequential prompt wizard was rejected because users cannot efficiently review and revise a complete physical definition."

